  bootwright / cluster exec
      Run a command over SSH on cluster nodes' Machines as the Machine's resolved identity;
      confirm or refuse an unproved host key and return the client's exit status. The session
      runs as the identity the Machine's desired state authorizes, over a host key proved
      before any credential is offered; an unproved key is confirmed interactively or refused.
      The exit status is the client's. Bootwright flags go before the command. Use -- before a
      flag-shaped first payload value to preserve it as data. After the first payload value,
      all remaining tokens belong to the payload. --name takes a comma-separated list, and each
      cluster runs the command on the Machine behind its first node in name order. --node takes
      a comma-separated list and selects those nodes, by name then by FQDN, in every listed
      cluster that declares them. The command runs on every resolved Machine at once, each
      output line is prefixed by its Machine, and the exit status is the highest any client
      returned. External StorageClusters are inapplicable, and sessions on OpenShift/OKD
      ContainerClusters are not yet available.

  Usage
    bootwright cluster exec <command>... [flags]

  Command flags
      --name  Select comma-separated cluster names (required)
      --node  Select declared nodes by comma-separated name, then FQDN (default: each cluster's
              first node in name order)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright cluster exec --context lab --name storage -- uname -a
